('f12fe4bd-d47d-5683-924a-373eaabc6ff1','72c02b37-4b29-5dda-a107-ce02529a172b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to deliberately pay no attention to something that you have been told or that you know about',null,null,'بی‌اعتنا بودن، نادیده گرفتن (تذکر)؛ تخطی نکردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"You can’t ignore the fact that many criminals never go to prison.","translation":"شما نمی توانید این واقعیت را نادیده بگیرید که بسیاری از جنایتکاران هرگز به زندان نمی روند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001750368.mp3"},{"sentence":"problems which we can’t afford to ignore","translation":"مشکلاتی که نمی توانیم نادیده بگیریم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001400043.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('0f436e4d-de36-504e-881c-222b4d1ea1d5','72c02b37-4b29-5dda-a107-ce02529a172b',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to behave as if you had not heard or seen someone or something',null,null,'طوری رفتار کنید که انگار کسی یا چیزی را نشنیده اید یا ندیده اید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The phone rang, but she ignored it.","translation":"تلفن زنگ خورد، اما او به آن توجهی نکرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001400038.mp3"},{"sentence":"Sam rudely ignored the question.","translation":"سام بی ادبانه به این سوال توجهی نکرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001400039.mp3"},{"sentence":"He had completely ignored her remark, preferring his own theory.","translation":"او اظهارات او را کاملاً نادیده گرفته بود و نظریه خود را ترجیح داد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001750374.mp3"},{"sentence":"There are signs telling you not to smoke, but people don’t take any notice of them.","translation":"علائمی وجود دارد که به شما می گوید سیگار نکشید، اما مردم هیچ توجهی به آنها نمی کنند.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,4),
('a3bfb168-7b61-59ed-888a-bec176ee84b3','9fc63ceb-660b-596b-85b7-ff3231e20830',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the effect or influence that an event , situation etc has on someone or something','[ countable ]',null,'تأثیر، برخورد (فیزیکی)؛ برخورد (سنگین)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['big/great Winning this competition could have a big impact on my life. His impact was greater than that of the Beatles.','huge/enormous/massive Industry has a huge impact on the environment we live in. The impact has been enormous on people’s daily lives.','small New technologies have only had a small impact on the overall level of employment.','minimal/negligible (= very small and not important ) The change in government had a minimal impact in the rural areas of the country.','positive (= having a good effect ) Cuts in federal spending should have a positive impact on America’s economic future.','negative/damaging (= having a bad effect ) The expansion of the airport would have a negative impact on the environment.','disastrous (= a very bad effect ) His leg injury had a disastrous impact on his career as a footballer.','a major/significant impact (= important ) The war had a major impact on French domestic politics.','a profound impact (= very important ) Population growth has a profound impact on world food demand.','an adverse impact formal (= a bad effect ) The loss of forests has had an adverse impact on bird populations.','a real impact informal (= a big impact ) The film made a real impact on cinema audiences.','a lasting impact (= one that lasts for a long time ) The arrival of the railways made a lasting impact on many sectors of the economy.','a long-term impact Scientists are calculating the long-term impact of the floods.','a short-term/immediate impact A military attack may only have a short-term impact on terrorist activity.','an emotional/psychological impact Their mother’s death had a huge emotional impact on the children.','an economic impact It is difficult to measure the economic impact of the war.','an environmental impact The environmental impact of the construction project is being investigated.','the full impact of something South Wales felt the full impact of the recession.','the potential/likely impact He’s studying the potential impact of climate change.','have an impact New technology has had a massive impact on our lives.','make an impact The product quickly made an impact on the market.','feel the impact of something The industry has felt the impact of rising fuel prices.','reduce/lessen/soften the impact of something (= make it less severe or unpleasant ) The chemical industry is looking at ways to reduce its impact on the environment.','lose impact (= have less effect ) The picture loses impact when it is reduced in size.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"We need to assess the impact on climate change.","translation":"ما باید تاثیر آن بر تغییرات آب و هوایی را ارزیابی کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001834183.mp3"},{"sentence":"Higher mortgage rates have already had a major impact on spending.","translation":"نرخ های بالاتر وام مسکن قبلاً تأثیر زیادی بر هزینه ها داشته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001719302.mp3"},{"sentence":"an international meeting to consider the environmental impacts of global warming","translation":"یک نشست بین المللی برای بررسی اثرات زیست محیطی گرمایش جهانی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001719310.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('fd363f57-b528-5eac-8cd0-104cf4a33d62','9fc63ceb-660b-596b-85b7-ff3231e20830',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the force of one object hitting another','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'نیروی برخورد یک جسم به جسم دیگر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['big/great Winning this competition could have a big impact on my life. His impact was greater than that of the Beatles.','huge/enormous/massive Industry has a huge impact on the environment we live in. The impact has been enormous on people’s daily lives.','small New technologies have only had a small impact on the overall level of employment.','minimal/negligible (= very small and not important ) The change in government had a minimal impact in the rural areas of the country.','positive (= having a good effect ) Cuts in federal spending should have a positive impact on America’s economic future.','negative/damaging (= having a bad effect ) The expansion of the airport would have a negative impact on the environment.','disastrous (= a very bad effect ) His leg injury had a disastrous impact on his career as a footballer.','a major/significant impact (= important ) The war had a major impact on French domestic politics.','a profound impact (= very important ) Population growth has a profound impact on world food demand.','an adverse impact formal (= a bad effect ) The loss of forests has had an adverse impact on bird populations.','a real impact informal (= a big impact ) The film made a real impact on cinema audiences.','a lasting impact (= one that lasts for a long time ) The arrival of the railways made a lasting impact on many sectors of the economy.','a long-term impact Scientists are calculating the long-term impact of the floods.','a short-term/immediate impact A military attack may only have a short-term impact on terrorist activity.','an emotional/psychological impact Their mother’s death had a huge emotional impact on the children.','an economic impact It is difficult to measure the economic impact of the war.','an environmental impact The environmental impact of the construction project is being investigated.','the full impact of something South Wales felt the full impact of the recession.','the potential/likely impact He’s studying the potential impact of climate change.','have an impact New technology has had a massive impact on our lives.','make an impact The product quickly made an impact on the market.','feel the impact of something The industry has felt the impact of rising fuel prices.','reduce/lessen/soften the impact of something (= make it less severe or unpleasant ) The chemical industry is looking at ways to reduce its impact on the environment.','lose impact (= have less effect ) The picture loses impact when it is reduced in size.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The force of the impact knocked the breath out of her.","translation":"نیروی ضربه نفس او را بیرون زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001404026.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('e52314e6-00f7-5ec5-bf1c-baadc722e6fc','9fc63ceb-660b-596b-85b7-ff3231e20830',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'on impact','تأثیر، برخورد (فیزیکی)؛ برخورد (سنگین)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['big/great Winning this competition could have a big impact on my life. His impact was greater than that of the Beatles.','huge/enormous/massive Industry has a huge impact on the environment we live in. The impact has been enormous on people’s daily lives.','small New technologies have only had a small impact on the overall level of employment.','minimal/negligible (= very small and not important ) The change in government had a minimal impact in the rural areas of the country.','positive (= having a good effect ) Cuts in federal spending should have a positive impact on America’s economic future.','negative/damaging (= having a bad effect ) The expansion of the airport would have a negative impact on the environment.','disastrous (= a very bad effect ) His leg injury had a disastrous impact on his career as a footballer.','a major/significant impact (= important ) The war had a major impact on French domestic politics.','a profound impact (= very important ) Population growth has a profound impact on world food demand.','an adverse impact formal (= a bad effect ) The loss of forests has had an adverse impact on bird populations.','a real impact informal (= a big impact ) The film made a real impact on cinema audiences.','a lasting impact (= one that lasts for a long time ) The arrival of the railways made a lasting impact on many sectors of the economy.','a long-term impact Scientists are calculating the long-term impact of the floods.','a short-term/immediate impact A military attack may only have a short-term impact on terrorist activity.','an emotional/psychological impact Their mother’s death had a huge emotional impact on the children.','an economic impact It is difficult to measure the economic impact of the war.','an environmental impact The environmental impact of the construction project is being investigated.','the full impact of something South Wales felt the full impact of the recession.','the potential/likely impact He’s studying the potential impact of climate change.','have an impact New technology has had a massive impact on our lives.','make an impact The product quickly made an impact on the market.','feel the impact of something The industry has felt the impact of rising fuel prices.','reduce/lessen/soften the impact of something (= make it less severe or unpleasant ) The chemical industry is looking at ways to reduce its impact on the environment.','lose impact (= have less effect ) The picture loses impact when it is reduced in size.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('b94881e6-03d2-5463-bc1f-125816e5e969','75fdc27d-ed29-50f5-9f50-4f58031aa2df',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to have an important or noticeable effect on someone or something',null,null,'تأثیر مهم یا محسوس بر کسی یا چیزی','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The Food Safety Act will progressively impact on the way food businesses operate.","translation":"قانون ایمنی مواد غذایی به تدریج بر نحوه فعالیت مشاغل مواد غذایی تأثیر می گذارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001404045.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('d60c1bb7-1bca-51c9-bfe2-bed6436f5fd7','b7b59311-fe93-5d73-bc1f-5fc587a74d88',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a product that is brought from one country into another so that it can be sold there, or the business of doing this','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'واردات، کالای وارداتی؛ اهمیت (درباره مضمون)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['foreign imports Foreign imports into Britain continued to grow in the 1970s.','cheap imports Farmers are complaining about cheap imports flooding the market.','Japanese/French etc imports (= goods from Japan, France etc ) Japanese imports rose by 5% last year.','oil/coal/food imports The country is dependent on oil imports for almost all its basic energy needs.','rice/sugar etc imports There is pressure on the country to reduce its rice imports.','agricultural imports Restrictions on agricultural imports remain in place.','essential imports The country had problems paying for its essential imports.','luxury imports Higher duties were placed on luxury imports.','increase imports The company increased imports in order to cut domestic production costs.','reduce/cut imports New investment will reduce imports and save jobs.','control/restrict imports (= reduce or put a limit on them ) The scheme aims to control imports of cheap goods.','ban imports (= make them illegal ) The organization wants the government to ban imports of exotic birds.','imports increase/rise/grow Imports increased by 13 percent last year.','imports fall/drop Imports of consumer goods fell sharply in December.','an import ban The US imposed an import ban on several types of fish.','import restrictions/controls (= laws which reduce or limit the amount of imports ) Severe import controls were introduced.','import quotas (= limits on the number of imports allowed ) Each country introduced its own import quotas.','import taxes/duties/tariffs The US imposed huge import duties on products from Europe.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a ban on beef imports","translation":"ممنوعیت واردات گوشت گاو","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001406922.mp3"},{"sentence":"the abolition of import duties (= taxes )","translation":"لغو عوارض واردات (= مالیات)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709427.mp3"},{"sentence":"cheap imports from Asia","translation":"واردات ارزان از آسیا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709433.mp3"},{"sentence":"American demand for Japanese imports (= goods from Japan )","translation":"تقاضای آمریکا برای واردات ژاپنی (= کالا از ژاپن)","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709434.mp3"},{"sentence":"the import of electrical goods","translation":"واردات کالاهای برقی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709437.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('38e942ad-b7ef-5452-b2f5-34077df35c38','b7b59311-fe93-5d73-bc1f-5fc587a74d88',2,null,null,'spoken & written','something new or different that is brought to a place where it did not previously exist','[ countable ]',null,'چیزی جدید یا متفاوت که به جایی آورده می شود که قبلا وجود نداشته است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['foreign imports Foreign imports into Britain continued to grow in the 1970s.','cheap imports Farmers are complaining about cheap imports flooding the market.','Japanese/French etc imports (= goods from Japan, France etc ) Japanese imports rose by 5% last year.','oil/coal/food imports The country is dependent on oil imports for almost all its basic energy needs.','rice/sugar etc imports There is pressure on the country to reduce its rice imports.','agricultural imports Restrictions on agricultural imports remain in place.','essential imports The country had problems paying for its essential imports.','luxury imports Higher duties were placed on luxury imports.','increase imports The company increased imports in order to cut domestic production costs.','reduce/cut imports New investment will reduce imports and save jobs.','control/restrict imports (= reduce or put a limit on them ) The scheme aims to control imports of cheap goods.','ban imports (= make them illegal ) The organization wants the government to ban imports of exotic birds.','imports increase/rise/grow Imports increased by 13 percent last year.','imports fall/drop Imports of consumer goods fell sharply in December.','an import ban The US imposed an import ban on several types of fish.','import restrictions/controls (= laws which reduce or limit the amount of imports ) Severe import controls were introduced.','import quotas (= limits on the number of imports allowed ) Each country introduced its own import quotas.','import taxes/duties/tariffs The US imposed huge import duties on products from Europe.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The beetle is thought to be a European import.","translation":"تصور می شود که سوسک وارداتی اروپایی باشد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709443.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('29409daa-f095-5229-96fb-b33025bf208d','b7b59311-fe93-5d73-bc1f-5fc587a74d88',3,null,null,'formal','importance or meaning','[ uncountable ]',null,'اهمیت یا معنا','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['foreign imports Foreign imports into Britain continued to grow in the 1970s.','cheap imports Farmers are complaining about cheap imports flooding the market.','Japanese/French etc imports (= goods from Japan, France etc ) Japanese imports rose by 5% last year.','oil/coal/food imports The country is dependent on oil imports for almost all its basic energy needs.','rice/sugar etc imports There is pressure on the country to reduce its rice imports.','agricultural imports Restrictions on agricultural imports remain in place.','essential imports The country had problems paying for its essential imports.','luxury imports Higher duties were placed on luxury imports.','increase imports The company increased imports in order to cut domestic production costs.','reduce/cut imports New investment will reduce imports and save jobs.','control/restrict imports (= reduce or put a limit on them ) The scheme aims to control imports of cheap goods.','ban imports (= make them illegal ) The organization wants the government to ban imports of exotic birds.','imports increase/rise/grow Imports increased by 13 percent last year.','imports fall/drop Imports of consumer goods fell sharply in December.','an import ban The US imposed an import ban on several types of fish.','import restrictions/controls (= laws which reduce or limit the amount of imports ) Severe import controls were introduced.','import quotas (= limits on the number of imports allowed ) Each country introduced its own import quotas.','import taxes/duties/tariffs The US imposed huge import duties on products from Europe.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a matter of no great import","translation":"موضوعی که اهمیت زیادی ندارد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001406938.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('e3e6ff37-8c61-55bb-b06a-d56c52bbc2b0','17f7ac7f-3389-5fdc-8d50-02790de86b35',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to bring a product from one country into another so that it can be sold there',null,null,'محصولی را از یک کشور به کشور دیگر بیاورند تا در آنجا فروخته شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"In 2001, Britain exported more cars than it imported.","translation":"در سال 2001، بریتانیا بیش از واردات خودرو صادر کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709445.mp3"},{"sentence":"All the meat is imported from France.","translation":"تمامی گوشت ها از فرانسه وارد می شود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709448.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('986eee4e-5e0c-5ee7-86c4-170eaac1ad9a','17f7ac7f-3389-5fdc-8d50-02790de86b35',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to introduce something new or different in a place where it did not previously exist',null,null,'معرفی چیزی جدید یا متفاوت در مکانی که قبلا وجود نداشته است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The unusual designs were probably imported from Iran.","translation":"طرح های غیر معمول احتمالا از ایران وارد شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709452.mp3"},{"sentence":"The US comedy format was gradually imported to UK screens.","translation":"قالب کمدی ایالات متحده به تدریج به نمایشگرهای بریتانیا وارد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709455.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('12456098-ba14-512a-b9c8-b295be303416','17f7ac7f-3389-5fdc-8d50-02790de86b35',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to move information from one computer to another',null,null,'برای انتقال اطلاعات از یک کامپیوتر به کامپیوتر دیگر','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"You can now import graphics from other applications.","translation":"اکنون می توانید گرافیک را از برنامه های دیگر وارد کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001709459.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('d280ab94-8184-58bd-9113-d36a70e9eecb','5e8dc338-d56b-535d-b314-d98230b227c3',1,null,null,'spoken & written','if someone in authority imposes a rule , punishment , tax etc, they force people to accept it','[ transitive ]',null,'تحمیل کردن، اجبار کردن (قانون، جریمه)؛ مهربان (بورس)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The court can impose a fine.","translation":"دادگاه می تواند جریمه کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001407144.mp3"},{"sentence":"The government imposed a ban on the sale of ivory.","translation":"دولت ممنوعیت فروش عاج را وضع کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001407143.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('7a6ada3a-98d1-5122-ad02-dbe989f5ed3f','5e8dc338-d56b-535d-b314-d98230b227c3',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to force someone to have the same ideas, beliefs etc as you','[ transitive ]',null,'مجبور کردن کسی به داشتن همان عقاید، عقاید و غیره با شما','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"parents who impose their own moral values on their children","translation":"والدینی که ارزش های اخلاقی خود را به فرزندانشان تحمیل می کنند","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001407156.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('7d6eadeb-058f-57fb-82b5-09821db14b34','5e8dc338-d56b-535d-b314-d98230b227c3',3,null,null,'formal','to expect or ask someone to do something for you when this is not convenient for them','[ intransitive ]',null,'انتظار داشته باشید یا از کسی بخواهید کاری برای شما انجام دهد در حالی که این برای او راحت نیست','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"We could ask to stay the night, but I don’t want to impose on them.","translation":"می‌توانیم بخواهیم شب بمانیم، اما نمی‌خواهم به آنها تحمیل کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001407163.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1fd8bffc-9b16-58a2-8093-4efe6e45a5bd','5e8dc338-d56b-535d-b314-d98230b227c3',4,null,null,'spoken & written','to have a bad effect on something or someone and to cause problems for them','[ transitive ]',null,'بر چیزی یا کسی تأثیر بد بگذارد و برای او مشکل ایجاد کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Military spending imposes a huge strain on the economy.","translation":"هزینه های نظامی فشار زیادی را بر اقتصاد تحمیل می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001407149.mp3"},{"sentence":"The government put a higher tax on cigarettes.","translation":"دولت مالیات بیشتری بر سیگار وضع کرده است.","audio_url":null},{"sentence":"This puts a lot of strain on families.","translation":"این موضوع فشار زیادی به خانواده ها وارد می کند.","audio_url":null}]'::jsonb,3),
('f5f070f2-3b2a-5ce2-ad94-6360a9046cc8','16800c8d-825d-5db4-bd0c-098f6d512c4e',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the money that you earn from your work or that you receive from investment s , the government etc',null,null,'درآمد، عایدی؛ درآمد (سالی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['have an income ( also receive an income formal ) We have an income of over $100,000 a year.','provide an income The properties he rented out provided him with an income.','generate an income (= provide one ) He decided to invest the money to generate an income for the future.','increase your income She took on extra work to increase her income.','supplement/add to your income (= increase your income, for example by doing an extra job ) Ted supplemented his income by doing part-time work in the evenings.','somebody’s income rises/increases/goes up They saw their income rise considerably over the next few years.','somebody’s income falls/goes down Average income fell by one third during this period.','a high/large income He has a relatively high income.','a low/small income Rent takes a large chunk of their small income.','somebody’s annual income Brian’s annual income is around £43,000.','the average income The report compares average incomes across different European countries.','the national income (= the income of a country ) A large proportion of the national income comes from food exports.','family/household income She works in a shop to supplement the family income.','disposable income (= your income after tax and necessary bills have been paid ) People spend a high proportion of their disposable income running a car.','gross income (= income before you have paid tax ) The family’s gross income has increased by 5% this year.','net income (= income after you have paid tax ) He was left with a net income of just £80 per week.','taxable income (= the part of your income on which you pay tax ) Money received in rent is included as part of your taxable income.','a joint income (= that two or more people have ) Between them they have a joint income of less than £20,000.','somebody''s personal income Average personal incomes rose by about 5% last year.','investment income (= income from investments ) You will be taxed on your investment income.','an income level/group The tax rate rises with the individual’s income level.','an income bracket (= income level ) In general, people in higher income brackets live longer.','income tax (= tax that you pay on your income ) The standard rate of income tax is to be cut by 0.5%.','incomes policy British English (= government controls on wages ) Government control of the economy must include an effective incomes policy.','a source of income His pension was his only source of income.','loss of income You can buy insurance to protect you against loss of income if you are ill.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"People on higher incomes should pay more tax.","translation":"افرادی که درآمد بیشتری دارند باید مالیات بیشتری بپردازند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa000838.mp3"},{"sentence":"income from savings and pensions","translation":"درآمد حاصل از پس انداز و مستمری","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001973112.mp3"},{"sentence":"low-income families","translation":"خانواده های کم درآمد","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001973095.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('28891431-0994-50ea-8423-ccd06c53be93','11680cd4-d88a-52cf-bb8b-bf5ce3f81369',1,null,null,'spoken & written','used to emphasize a statement or answer','[ sentence adverb ]',null,'واقعاً، حق با شماست؛ در حقیقت (تأکید)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The blood tests prove that Vince is indeed the father.","translation":"آزمایش خون ثابت می کند که وینس واقعا پدر است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001733554.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘Would it help if you had an assistant?’ ‘It would indeed.’","translation":"«اگر دستیار داشتی کمکی می‌کرد؟» «در واقع این کار را می‌کرد.»","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001376039.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('b149313e-df41-50ec-bff4-afe2a7f61e78','11680cd4-d88a-52cf-bb8b-bf5ce3f81369',2,null,null,'formal','used to introduce an additional statement that emphasizes or supports what you have just said','[ sentence adverb ]',null,'برای معرفی یک بیانیه اضافی که بر آنچه شما گفتید تأکید یا پشتیبانی می کند استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"I didn’t mind at all. Indeed, I was pleased.","translation":"اصلا برام مهم نبود راستی من راضی بودم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001376045.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('de365b63-0893-55dd-810e-2462626b47cc','11680cd4-d88a-52cf-bb8b-bf5ce3f81369',3,null,null,'spoken & written','used with ‘very’ and an adjective or adverb to emphasize a statement or description',null,null,'با "خیلی" و یک صفت یا قید برای تأکید بر یک عبارت یا توصیف استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Most of the essays were very good indeed.","translation":"بیشتر انشاها واقعاً خوب بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001733555.mp3"},{"sentence":"Thank you very much indeed.","translation":"واقعا ازت ممنونم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001376052.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('fc60d054-32f6-5a00-a56f-c1906690ac9c','11680cd4-d88a-52cf-bb8b-bf5ce3f81369',4,null,null,'spoken','used to show that you are surprised or annoyed by something that someone has just told you',null,null,'برای نشان دادن اینکه از چیزی که کسی به تازگی به شما گفته است متعجب یا عصبانی هستید استفاده می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"‘He said he was too busy to see you.’ ‘Did he, indeed?’","translation":"او گفت که برای دیدن شما سرش شلوغ است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001376060.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('147ccbd8-5b5f-511a-8b49-204371254dc5','11680cd4-d88a-52cf-bb8b-bf5ce3f81369',5,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'why/how/who etc indeed?','واقعاً، حق با شماست؛ در حقیقت (تأکید)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('0eb9327a-9859-5386-ad4f-81e4518d465d','fc2a50a2-6c42-5e02-ad4d-eaee5061fc08',1,null,null,'formal','a baby or very young child','[ countable ]','Sudden Infant Death Syndrome','نوزاد، خردسال؛ نوپا (سپاه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a young infant The never-ending demands of a young infant can be very stressful for parents.','a newborn infant Newborn infants only a few hours old can distinguish between different voices.','an unborn infant Unborn infants can hear certain sounds while still in the mother’s womb.','a premature infant (= born too early ) The hospital provides life-saving care to premature infants.','a healthy infant Amy gave birth to a healthy infant.','a sick infant Sick infants are treated in the intensive care nursery.','infant deaths The number of infant deaths has fallen significantly.','infant mortality (= the number of infants who die ) The infant mortality rate doubled during the 1990s.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"An infant’s skin is very sensitive.","translation":"پوست نوزاد بسیار حساس است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001727993.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
