('bcddea35-b12b-52a2-9337-035164d4860c','541e7753-a7e0-5e98-810b-78580930024c',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a person or country that belongs to a group or organization',null,null,'عضو، موظف (گروه)؛ عضو (پیکر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be a member of something Lisa is a member of the hockey team.','become a member Germany became a member of N.A.T.O. in 1954.','a committee/staff/family etc member Close friendships developed between crew members on the ship.','a leading member (= an important member ) a discussion between leading members of the profession','a senior/junior member (= with a higher or lower rank ) A senior member of the government has resigned.','an active member (= one who takes part in many activities of an organization ) She was an active member of the church.','a founder member (= one who helped start an organization ) He was a founder member of the African National Congress.','a staff member He became a staff member of the Institute in 2002.','a full member (= one who has all the possible rights of a member ) At that time, women were not allowed to be full members of the club.','an associate member (= one who has fewer rights than a full member ) Turkey is an associate member of the European Union.','a card-carrying member ( also a paid-up member British English ) (= an official member of an organization ) She was a card-carrying member of the Communist Party.','a life member (= one who has paid to be a member for their whole life ) a life member of the Royal Academy of Artists','an honorary member (= one who has been given membership as an honour ) He was made an honorary member of the Botanical Society.','a member of a committee/of staff etc All members of staff attend regular training sessions.','a member of the public Members of the public were invited to put forward suggestions.','a member of society (= a citizen ) We want our children to become productive members of society.','a member state/country/nation (= a country that belongs to an international organization ) the member states of the European Union']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The majority of union members voted in favour of a strike.","translation":"اکثریت اعضای اتحادیه به اعتصاب رای مثبت دادند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000221270.mp3"},{"sentence":"You can also invite members of your family.","translation":"شما همچنین می توانید اعضای خانواده خود را دعوت کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001023.mp3"},{"sentence":"He is a member of the local tennis club.","translation":"او عضو باشگاه تنیس محلی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001628076.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('22bc94c1-f6bf-5717-b75d-71fe7c8ded7a','541e7753-a7e0-5e98-810b-78580930024c',2,null,null,'spoken & written','one of a particular group of animals or plants',null,null,'یکی از گروه خاصی از حیوانات یا گیاهان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['be a member of something Lisa is a member of the hockey team.','become a member Germany became a member of N.A.T.O. in 1954.','a committee/staff/family etc member Close friendships developed between crew members on the ship.','a leading member (= an important member ) a discussion between leading members of the profession','a senior/junior member (= with a higher or lower rank ) A senior member of the government has resigned.','an active member (= one who takes part in many activities of an organization ) She was an active member of the church.','a founder member (= one who helped start an organization ) He was a founder member of the African National Congress.','a staff member He became a staff member of the Institute in 2002.','a full member (= one who has all the possible rights of a member ) At that time, women were not allowed to be full members of the club.','an associate member (= one who has fewer rights than a full member ) Turkey is an associate member of the European Union.','a card-carrying member ( also a paid-up member British English ) (= an official member of an organization ) She was a card-carrying member of the Communist Party.','a life member (= one who has paid to be a member for their whole life ) a life member of the Royal Academy of Artists','an honorary member (= one who has been given membership as an honour ) He was made an honorary member of the Botanical Society.','a member of a committee/of staff etc All members of staff attend regular training sessions.','a member of the public Members of the public were invited to put forward suggestions.','a member of society (= a citizen ) We want our children to become productive members of society.','a member state/country/nation (= a country that belongs to an international organization ) the member states of the European Union']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The plant is a member of the lily family .","translation":"این گیاه از خانواده سوسن است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001974086.mp3"},{"sentence":"Wolves and domestic dogs are members of the same species .","translation":"گرگ ها و سگ های اهلی اعضای یک گونه هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001628085.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
