('2e600c1b-b333-598d-8707-e18b51a33d4d','278a654a-aa6a-5a1d-a07e-edd68fb8170e',1,'ability to remember','توانایی به خاطر سپردن','spoken & written','someone’s ability to remember things, places, experiences etc','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'حافظه؛ خاطره؛ حافظه (رایانه)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['good/excellent I wish my memory was as good as yours.','bad/poor/terrible A student with a poor memory may struggle in school.','short-term memory (= your ability to remember things that you have just seen, heard, or done ) The drug can damage your short-term memory.','long-term memory (= your ability to remember things that happened a long time ago ) Most people''s long-term memory is limited.','visual memory (= your ability to remember things you have seen ) Poor spellers often have a weak visual memory.','a photographic memory (= the ability to remember every detail of things that you have seen ) Unless you have a photographic memory, you forget half of what you read as soon as you close the book.','remain/stay/stick in your memory (= be remembered for a long time ) That day will remain in my memory forever.','refresh/jog your memory (= help someone to remember something ) Perhaps this photograph will refresh your memory?','lose your memory (= become unable to remember things that happened in the past ) The blow on the head caused him to lose his memory.','commit something to memory formal (= make yourself remember something ) I''ve already committed his name to memory.','have a short memory (= if you have a short memory, you soon forget things ) Voters have short memories.','have a long memory (= if you have a long memory, you remember things for a long time ) He has a long memory for people who have let him down.','have a memory like a sieve (= forget things very easily ) I''m sorry, I have a memory like a sieve. I forgot you were coming today!','loss of memory/memory loss (= when you cannot remember things ) The condition can cause dizziness and memory loss.','a lapse of memory/a memory lapse (= when you cannot remember something for a short time ) The alcohol seemed to make him suffer lapses of memory.','if my memory serves (me correctly/right) (= used to say that you are almost certain you have remembered something correctly ) If my memory serves me correctly, Johnson was also there.','something is etched in your memory (= it is impossible to forget ) The date was etched in my memory.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"She has a terrible memory for names.","translation":"او حافظه وحشتناکی برای اسامی دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000221541.mp3"},{"sentence":"The pianist played the whole piece from memory.","translation":"پیانیست تمام قطعه را از حفظ می نواخت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000221548.mp3"},{"sentence":"The image has remained in my memory ever since.","translation":"تصویر از آن زمان در حافظه من باقی مانده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001974164.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('25128e06-0482-5911-b990-e4574639e476','278a654a-aa6a-5a1d-a07e-edd68fb8170e',2,'something you remember','چیزی که به یاد می آوری','spoken & written','something that you remember from the past about a person, place, or experience','[ countable usually plural ]',null,'چیزی که از گذشته در مورد یک شخص، مکان یا تجربه به یاد می آورید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She talked about her memories of the war.","translation":"او از خاطراتش از جنگ گفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000221556.mp3"},{"sentence":"He has lots of happy memories of his stay in Japan.","translation":"او خاطرات خوشی از اقامتش در ژاپن دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000221559.mp3"},{"sentence":"When I saw the pictures, the memories came flooding back (= I suddenly had many memories about something ) .","translation":"وقتی عکس ها را دیدم، خاطرات دوباره سرازیر شدند (= ناگهان خاطرات زیادی در مورد چیزی پیدا کردم).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040132.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('ef48bcd6-5548-54e2-90c4-f208f019ed39','278a654a-aa6a-5a1d-a07e-edd68fb8170e',3,'computer','کامپیوتر','spoken & written','the part of a computer where information can be stored','[ countable ]',null,'بخشی از کامپیوتر که اطلاعات را می توان در آن ذخیره کرد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The data is stored in the computer’s memory.","translation":"داده ها در حافظه کامپیوتر ذخیره می شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564120.mp3"},{"sentence":"128 Mb of memory","translation":"128 مگابایت حافظه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000221577.mp3"},{"sentence":"Personal computers now have much increased memory capacity.","translation":"رایانه های شخصی اکنون ظرفیت حافظه بسیار افزایش یافته ای دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001564122.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
