('28dbb0ef-40d4-53a0-b14d-4bef04a483c1','9c40151b-f4dc-50cd-b1ab-a2bc2ea722f7',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a city which is Alabama''s only port and one of the busiest ports in the US',null,null,'شهری که تنها بندر آلاباما و یکی از شلوغ ترین بنادر ایالات متحده است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('e2701274-0d7a-55e2-bb5f-4beca19e3199','c788069f-5f2a-52d3-bdb8-471fd4f49397',1,null,null,'spoken & written','belonging to the present time or most recent time','[ only before noun ]',null,'مدرن، نو؛ جدید (زمان)؛ نوپا (فرد)',array['contemporary']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the modern world The island has hardly been affected by the modern world.','modern society In modern society, elderly relatives rarely live with their children.','modern times It was one of the greatest disasters of modern times.','the modern age/era/period (= now, rather than in the past ) In the modern age, television is the main means of mass communication.','modern life These problems are a major part of modern life.','modern man (= people today ) Modern man gets much less exercise in his daily life than his ancestors.','modern history British English (= recent history, as a subject of study ) a degree in modern history','modern languages British English (= languages that are spoken today, as a subject of study ) French, German and other modern languages','the modern equivalent of something (= something with the same importance or purpose as something from the past ) In their own minds they are the modern equivalent of highwaymen.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Such companies must change if they are to compete in the modern world .","translation":"چنین شرکت هایی برای رقابت در دنیای مدرن باید تغییر کنند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648395.mp3"},{"sentence":"They are the youngest children in modern times to face murder charges.","translation":"آنها کوچکترین کودکان در دوران مدرن هستند که با اتهامات قتل روبرو هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001764006.mp3"},{"sentence":"Smaller families are a feature of modern society .","translation":"خانواده های کوچک از ویژگی های جامعه مدرن هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000204920.mp3"},{"sentence":"Computers are an essential part of modern life .","translation":"کامپیوترها بخش مهمی از زندگی مدرن هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648390.mp3"},{"sentence":"a book about modern history","translation":"کتابی در مورد تاریخ مدرن","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000204919.mp3"},{"sentence":"The original supermarkets were small by modern standards.","translation":"سوپرمارکت های اصلی با استانداردهای مدرن کوچک بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000204921.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('409c9eb1-f605-565b-b69e-f695a7b658d3','c788069f-5f2a-52d3-bdb8-471fd4f49397',2,null,null,'spoken & written','made or done using the most recent designs or methods',null,null,'با استفاده از جدیدترین طرح ها یا روش ها ساخته یا انجام شده است',array['up-to-date']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the modern world The island has hardly been affected by the modern world.','modern society In modern society, elderly relatives rarely live with their children.','modern times It was one of the greatest disasters of modern times.','the modern age/era/period (= now, rather than in the past ) In the modern age, television is the main means of mass communication.','modern life These problems are a major part of modern life.','modern man (= people today ) Modern man gets much less exercise in his daily life than his ancestors.','modern history British English (= recent history, as a subject of study ) a degree in modern history','modern languages British English (= languages that are spoken today, as a subject of study ) French, German and other modern languages','the modern equivalent of something (= something with the same importance or purpose as something from the past ) In their own minds they are the modern equivalent of highwaymen.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"A lot of progress has been made with the use of modern technology .","translation":"با استفاده از تکنولوژی مدرن پیشرفت های زیادی حاصل شده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648401.mp3"},{"sentence":"advances in modern medicine","translation":"پیشرفت در پزشکی مدرن","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648404.mp3"},{"sentence":"modern surgical techniques","translation":"تکنیک های مدرن جراحی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000204927.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('b90eedda-d7e2-5d46-8f65-96987195ec4b','c788069f-5f2a-52d3-bdb8-471fd4f49397',3,null,null,'spoken & written','modern art , music , literature etc uses styles that have been recently developed and are very different from traditional styles','[ only before noun ]',null,'هنر مدرن، موسیقی، ادبیات و غیره از سبک هایی استفاده می کند که اخیراً توسعه یافته اند و بسیار متفاوت از سبک های سنتی هستند',array['contemporary']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the modern world The island has hardly been affected by the modern world.','modern society In modern society, elderly relatives rarely live with their children.','modern times It was one of the greatest disasters of modern times.','the modern age/era/period (= now, rather than in the past ) In the modern age, television is the main means of mass communication.','modern life These problems are a major part of modern life.','modern man (= people today ) Modern man gets much less exercise in his daily life than his ancestors.','modern history British English (= recent history, as a subject of study ) a degree in modern history','modern languages British English (= languages that are spoken today, as a subject of study ) French, German and other modern languages','the modern equivalent of something (= something with the same importance or purpose as something from the past ) In their own minds they are the modern equivalent of highwaymen.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"an exhibition of modern art","translation":"نمایشگاهی از هنر مدرن","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648407.mp3"},{"sentence":"modern dance","translation":"رقص مدرن","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000204936.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('08001bb1-1a2a-5a8d-908f-d43bfd787edf','c788069f-5f2a-52d3-bdb8-471fd4f49397',4,null,null,'spoken & written','having very recent attitudes or ways of behaving',null,null,'داشتن نگرش ها یا شیوه های رفتاری بسیار جدید',array['progressive']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['the modern world The island has hardly been affected by the modern world.','modern society In modern society, elderly relatives rarely live with their children.','modern times It was one of the greatest disasters of modern times.','the modern age/era/period (= now, rather than in the past ) In the modern age, television is the main means of mass communication.','modern life These problems are a major part of modern life.','modern man (= people today ) Modern man gets much less exercise in his daily life than his ancestors.','modern history British English (= recent history, as a subject of study ) a degree in modern history','modern languages British English (= languages that are spoken today, as a subject of study ) French, German and other modern languages','the modern equivalent of something (= something with the same importance or purpose as something from the past ) In their own minds they are the modern equivalent of highwaymen.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The school is very modern in its approach to sex education.","translation":"این مدرسه در رویکرد خود به آموزش جنسی بسیار مدرن است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000204931.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('cd1ddd8e-ab20-5f29-b08f-92526cefff52','0434c56f-744f-5a52-b97c-ee1276f46d22',1,'point in time','نقطه در زمان','spoken & written','a particular point in time',null,null,'لحظه، دم؛ اهمیت (لحظه)؛ دم (بازی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['right/perfect I’m just waiting for the right moment to tell her. The moment is not quite right just yet.','an opportune moment (= a good time to do something ) I was waiting for an opportune moment to leave.','a historic moment (= a moment that is important in history ) The fall of the Berlin wall was a historic moment.','a memorable moment There have been many memorable moments in this year’s Olympics.','the exact/precise moment Her stomach chose that precise moment to make a loud noise.','the very moment (= used for emphasizing that something happened at a particular time ) I could tell something was wrong from the very moment I walked in through the front door.','the present moment (= now ) At the present moment, there are 500 students at the school.','an important moment This was probably the most important moment in his life.','a critical/crucial moment (= a very important moment ) This was a critical moment in the country’s history.','a defining moment (= something that shows the real character or purpose of something ) The win was a defining moment in the boxer’s career.','somebody’s finest moment (= when someone was most successful or admired ) The performance was one of the band’s finest moments.','somebody’s proudest moment (= when someone did the thing they are most proud of ) My proudest moment was when my daughter was born.','the worst moment Standing on the edge waiting to do your bungee jump is the worst moment.','capture the moment (= to take a picture, describe something etc that will remind you of a particular time ) They captured the moment on film.','enjoy the moment She found herself laughing with him, enjoying the moment.','savour the moment (= enjoy the moment ) He seemed to savour every moment of their conversation.','relive the moment (= experience something again by thinking about it, talking about it etc ) In court she had to relive the moment her son was murdered.','choose a moment to do something (= do something at a particular time ) She always seemed to choose the worst moment to interrupt his thoughts.','dread a moment (= feel anxious or worried about something that will happen ) She was dreading the moment when she would have to fire him.','just this/that moment (= only a very short time ago ) I had just that moment arrived.','at this moment in time (= now ) At this moment in time we cannot proceed with the proposal.','from that moment on (= after that time ) From that moment on I saw very little of Dean.','moment to moment/moment by moment (= used for emphasizing that something changes quickly ) The colours of the sunset changed moment to moment.','every waking moment (= all the time you are awake ) He spent every waking moment in the lab.','at a given moment (= at any particular time ) There was no variety at all - you knew exactly what you would be doing at any given moment of the week.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"It was one of the most exciting moments in his life.","translation":"این یکی از هیجان انگیزترین لحظات زندگی او بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648494.mp3"},{"sentence":"Just at that moment there was a knock on the door.","translation":"درست در همان لحظه در زده شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000205780.mp3"},{"sentence":"She may be in trouble at this very moment and trying to call you.","translation":"او ممکن است در همین لحظه دچار مشکل شود و سعی کند با شما تماس بگیرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000205781.mp3"},{"sentence":"I remember the moment when I first saw him after the operation.","translation":"لحظه ای را به یاد می آورم که اولین بار بعد از عمل او را دیدم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648490.mp3"},{"sentence":"Quinn always seems to be in the right place at the crucial moment.","translation":"به نظر می رسد کوین همیشه در لحظه حساس در مکان مناسب است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648495.mp3"},{"sentence":"I just this moment (= only a very short time ago ) arrived and already Dan wants to know when I’m leaving.","translation":"من همین لحظه (= فقط چند وقت پیش) رسیدم و از قبل دن می خواهد بداند که من کی می روم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000205789.mp3"},{"sentence":"At this moment in time it would be inappropriate to comment on the situation.","translation":"در این برهه زمانی اظهار نظر در مورد وضعیت نامناسب خواهد بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000205785.mp3"},{"sentence":"From that moment on (= after that time ) we were the best of friends.","translation":"از آن لحظه به بعد (= پس از آن زمان) ما بهترین دوستان بودیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648502.mp3"}]'::jsonb,8),
('f1baaedc-1b88-5716-892f-d40b69ab4830','0434c56f-744f-5a52-b97c-ee1276f46d22',2,'short time','زمان کوتاه','spoken & written','a very short period of time',null,null,'یک دوره زمانی بسیار کوتاه','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He was here a moment ago .","translation":"او چند لحظه پیش اینجا بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648506.mp3"},{"sentence":"Can you spare a few moments to answer some questions?","translation":"آیا می توانید چند لحظه برای پاسخ به برخی از سوالات وقت بگذارید؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000205796.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ll come back to that point in a moment.","translation":"من یک لحظه دیگر به آن نقطه باز خواهم گشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000205800.mp3"},{"sentence":"It was quiet for a moment, then Rae spoke.","translation":"یک لحظه ساکت شد، سپس رائه صحبت کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000205803.mp3"},{"sentence":"‘I don’t understand, ’ said Louise after a moment.","translation":"لوئیز بعد از لحظه ای گفت: \"نمی فهمم.\"","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648518.mp3"},{"sentence":"A moment later we heard a splash.","translation":"لحظه ای بعد صدایی شنیدیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648521.mp3"},{"sentence":"Just a moment; let me put these away first.","translation":"فقط یک لحظه؛ بگذارید اول اینها را کنار بگذارم","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000205807.mp3"},{"sentence":"We have to be ready to leave at a moment’s notice (= very quickly ) .","translation":"ما باید آماده حرکت در یک لحظه (= خیلی سریع) باشیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001648522.mp3"}]'::jsonb,8),
