('abd755d4-a952-553d-8bd1-9c86c11e0d65','f6cc8749-22c3-57d1-bfe1-d089ff4961c9',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to make something narrower, or to become narrower',null,null,'باریکتر کردن چیزی یا باریکتر شدن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"He narrowed his eyes and gazed at the horizon.","translation":"چشمانش را ریز کرد و به افق خیره شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000233408.mp3"},{"sentence":"The track divided into two and narrowed.","translation":"مسیر به دو قسمت تقسیم شد و باریک شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000233407.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('4d0c0119-674b-51ae-a617-8fc8f7498466','f6cc8749-22c3-57d1-bfe1-d089ff4961c9',2,null,null,'spoken & written','if a range, difference etc narrows, or if something narrows it, it becomes less',null,null,'اگر یک محدوده، تفاوت و غیره باریک شود، یا اگر چیزی آن را محدود کند، کمتر می شود','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The choice of goods available is narrowing.","translation":"انتخاب کالاهای موجود در حال محدود شدن است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000233418.mp3"},{"sentence":"The economic gap between the two halves of the country was beginning to narrow.","translation":"شکاف اقتصادی بین دو نیمه کشور در حال کاهش بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001535423.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('be1bff9a-5b46-58c5-9d73-8fbc7cb9ea82','819d39de-a66e-5248-9b17-7ff8ddc2f98a',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a country, considered especially in relation to its people and its social or economic structure',null,null,'ملت، ملت‌ساز (کشور)؛ ملت (مردم)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a great/powerful nation The United States is the most powerful nation in the world.','an independent/sovereign nation (= one that rules itself, rather than being run by another country ) Countries that were once colonies of Britain are now independent nations.','an industrial/industrialized nation The rich industrial nations dominate the global economy.','a developed/advanced nation (= one that has many industries ) In the developed nations, many students go on to university.','a developing/emerging nation (= one that is starting to have more industry ) Food shortages are often a problem in developing nations.','a rich/wealthy nation Most tourists come from the wealthy nations of the world.','a poor nation The high cost of medicines in poor nations prevents many citizens from receiving health care.','lead a nation He led the nation out of a depression and into a period of growth and prosperity.','face a nation There are many problems facing our nation.','unite a nation (= make everyone in a country agree ) The crisis seemed to unite the nation.','divide a nation (= make people in a nation disagree ) The war has divided the nation.','shock a nation (= make everyone in a nation feel shocked ) This terrible crime has shocked the whole nation.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the president’s radio broadcast to the nation","translation":"رادیو رئیس جمهور برای ملت پخش می شود","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000233723.mp3"},{"sentence":"an independent nation","translation":"یک ملت مستقل","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001535496.mp3"},{"sentence":"the world’s leading industrial nations","translation":"کشورهای صنعتی پیشرو جهان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001535499.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('d09788ee-9a39-5398-9da0-dd02f735d3d7','819d39de-a66e-5248-9b17-7ff8ddc2f98a',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a large group of people of the same race and language',null,null,'گروه بزرگی از مردم از یک نژاد و زبان','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a great/powerful nation The United States is the most powerful nation in the world.','an independent/sovereign nation (= one that rules itself, rather than being run by another country ) Countries that were once colonies of Britain are now independent nations.','an industrial/industrialized nation The rich industrial nations dominate the global economy.','a developed/advanced nation (= one that has many industries ) In the developed nations, many students go on to university.','a developing/emerging nation (= one that is starting to have more industry ) Food shortages are often a problem in developing nations.','a rich/wealthy nation Most tourists come from the wealthy nations of the world.','a poor nation The high cost of medicines in poor nations prevents many citizens from receiving health care.','lead a nation He led the nation out of a depression and into a period of growth and prosperity.','face a nation There are many problems facing our nation.','unite a nation (= make everyone in a country agree ) The crisis seemed to unite the nation.','divide a nation (= make people in a nation disagree ) The war has divided the nation.','shock a nation (= make everyone in a nation feel shocked ) This terrible crime has shocked the whole nation.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the Cherokee nation","translation":"ملت چروکی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000233728.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
