('f036e258-f501-5d2e-9634-a1b6892ca109','f91d4a75-c8a7-515d-bd2f-0dcb61a9b2bf',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the place or situation in which something begins to exist','[ plural ]',null,'خاستگاه، مبدأ؛ ریشه (کلمه)؛ مبدأ (شرکت)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a common origin (= a place or situation in which different things all started to exist ) It may be that all life on Earth has a common origin.','of recent origin (= having started to exist only a short time ago ) This particular theory is of very recent origin.','of unknown origin (= used to say that no one knows where, when, or how something started ) an ancient folk tale of unknown origin','of doubtful origin (= unknown and possibly suspicious ) The fire was still being treated as of doubtful origin.','something’s historical/geographical/political etc origins This type of story has its historical origins in eighteenth century gothic novels. the geographical origins of the plant','have its origin in something (= begin to exist ) The ceremony has its origins in medieval times.','trace its origins to something (= used to say that something can find evidence that it began to exist at a particular time or in a particular place ) The Roman Catholic Church traces its origins back to the 4th century.','trace the origin of something (= find where, when etc something began to exist ) It’s difficult to trace the origin of some words.','owe its origins to something (= used to explain how something began to exist ) a government which owes its origins to revolution','something’s origins lie in something (= something comes from a particular place or or develops from a particular situation ) a grape whose origins lie in northern Italy The technique’s origins lie in the popular arts of the time.','something’s origins go back to something (= used to say when or how something began ) The school’s origins go back to the 12th century.','investigate the origin of something (= try to find out where, when etc something began to exist ) researchers investigating the origin of AIDS','the country/place of origin (= the country or place where something is made or produced ) The rugs are somewhat cheaper in their country of origin.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a new theory to explain the origins of the universe","translation":"یک نظریه جدید برای توضیح منشاء جهان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000380033.mp3"},{"sentence":"Most coughs are viral in origin.","translation":"بیشتر سرفه ها منشا ویروسی دارند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001567094.mp3"},{"sentence":"The word is French in origin.","translation":"اصل این کلمه فرانسوی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001567095.mp3"},{"sentence":"The tradition has its origins in the Middle Ages.","translation":"این سنت ریشه در قرون وسطی دارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001567096.mp3"},{"sentence":"old folk tales of unknown origin","translation":"داستان های عامیانه قدیمی با منشأ ناشناخته","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001567102.mp3"},{"sentence":"All meat should be clearly labelled with its country of origin.","translation":"تمام گوشت ها باید به وضوح با کشور مبدا برچسب گذاری شوند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001567107.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
