hing began to exist ) researchers investigating the origin of AIDS','the country/place of origin (= the country or place where something is made or produced ) The rugs are somewhat cheaper in their country of origin.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Two thirds of the pupils are of Asian origin.","translation":"دو سوم دانش آموزان اصالتاً آسیایی هستند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001567111.mp3"},{"sentence":"The form asks for information about the person’s ethnic origin .","translation":"این فرم اطلاعاتی در مورد منشاء قومی فرد می خواهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001567112.mp3"},{"sentence":"Immigrants rarely return to their country of origin .","translation":"مهاجران به ندرت به کشور مبدا خود باز می گردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001567116.mp3"},{"sentence":"She never forgot her humble origins .","translation":"او هرگز خاستگاه فروتن خود را فراموش نکرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001567120.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
