('24408e9b-63ff-57f3-a010-5c0ad4486d71','5b2bdbae-9a63-5b71-af76-24bf785a5ee5',1,'in clothes','در لباس','spoken & written','a type of small bag in or on a coat , trousers etc that you can put money, keys etc in',null,null,'جیب، پاکت (لباس)؛ جیب (پول)؛ جیب (درس)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['put something in your pocket I put the £5 note in my pocket.','stuff/thrust something in your pocket (= put it there quickly and carelessly ) He took off his cap and stuffed it in his pocket.','take something out of/from your pocket Marcia took a pair of dark glasses out of her pocket.','reach into your pocket (= put your hand into your pocket to find something ) "Do you want a cigarette?" he asked, reaching into his pocket.','search your pocket (= look for something in your pocket ) I searched my pockets for my train ticket but it wasn''t there.','turn out/empty your pockets (= take everything out of your pockets in order to find something ) His mother made him turn out his pockets.','dig in your pocket (= put your hand in your pocket to find something ) Boris dug in his pocket for his keys.','with your hands in your pockets I saw him wandering along the beach with his hands in his pockets.','somebody''s pockets are bulging (= they are very full ) Tony''s pockets were bulging with loose change.','a back/front/side pocket He took a wad of money from his back pocket.','a breast pocket (= on the chest ) There was a silk handkerchief in his breast pocket.','an inside pocket (= on the inside of a coat, jacket etc ) Gregson pulled a photo from the inside pocket of his jacket.','a jacket/trouser/shirt etc pocket She slipped the map into her jacket pocket.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Luke came in with his hands in his pockets.","translation":"لوک با دست در جیب وارد شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001539466.mp3"},{"sentence":"The keys are in my trouser pocket.","translation":"کلیدها در جیب شلوار من است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000342613.mp3"},{"sentence":"the inside pocket of his jacket","translation":"جیب داخلی ژاکتش","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001539462.mp3"},{"sentence":"The policeman told me to turn out my pockets (= take everything out of them ) .","translation":"پلیس به من گفت که جیب هایم را بچرخانم (= همه چیز را از آنها بیرون بیاورم).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001539467.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('2120418c-b577-5be7-aeb6-62d0f1465830','5b2bdbae-9a63-5b71-af76-24bf785a5ee5',2,'money','پول','spoken & written','the amount of money that you have to spend',null,null,'مقدار پولی که باید خرج کنید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['put something in your pocket I put the £5 note in my pocket.','stuff/thrust something in your pocket (= put it there quickly and carelessly ) He took off his cap and stuffed it in his pocket.','take something out of/from your pocket Marcia took a pair of dark glasses out of her pocket.','reach into your pocket (= put your hand into your pocket to find something ) "Do you want a cigarette?" he asked, reaching into his pocket.','search your pocket (= look for something in your pocket ) I searched my pockets for my train ticket but it wasn''t there.','turn out/empty your pockets (= take everything out of your pockets in order to find something ) His mother made him turn out his pockets.','dig in your pocket (= put your hand in your pocket to find something ) Boris dug in his pocket for his keys.','with your hands in your pockets I saw him wandering along the beach with his hands in his pockets.','somebody''s pockets are bulging (= they are very full ) Tony''s pockets were bulging with loose change.','a back/front/side pocket He took a wad of money from his back pocket.','a breast pocket (= on the chest ) There was a silk handkerchief in his breast pocket.','an inside pocket (= on the inside of a coat, jacket etc ) Gregson pulled a photo from the inside pocket of his jacket.','a jacket/trouser/shirt etc pocket She slipped the map into her jacket pocket.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There are eight hotels, with a price range to suit every pocket .","translation":"هشت هتل وجود دارد، با محدوده قیمتی که مناسب هر جیب است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001539474.mp3"},{"sentence":"Dan had to pay for the repairs out of his own pocket.","translation":"دن مجبور شد هزینه تعمیرات را از جیب خودش بپردازد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001539481.mp3"},{"sentence":"He was accused of diverting some of the firm’s money into his own pocket.","translation":"او متهم شد که مقداری از پول شرکت را به جیب خودش می‌برد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001539487.mp3"},{"sentence":"The deepening recession has hit people’s pockets .","translation":"تشدید رکود به جیب مردم ضربه زده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000342623.mp3"},{"sentence":"For investors with deep pockets (= a lot of money ) , the Berlin property market is attractive.","translation":"برای سرمایه گذارانی که جیب های عمیق دارند (= پول زیاد)، بازار املاک برلین جذاب است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001539501.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('441d0872-62b7-57cf-906c-2171a21e6052','5b2bdbae-9a63-5b71-af76-24bf785a5ee5',3,'small container','ظرف کوچک','spoken & written','a small bag or piece of material fastened to something so that you can put things into it',null,null,'کیسه کوچک یا تکه ای از مواد که به چیزی بسته شده تا بتوانید چیزها را در آن قرار دهید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['put something in your pocket I put the £5 note in my pocket.','stuff/thrust something in your pocket (= put it there quickly and carelessly ) He took off his cap and stuffed it in his pocket.','take something out of/from your pocket Marcia took a pair of dark glasses out of her pocket.','reach into your pocket (= put your hand into your pocket to find something ) "Do you want a cigarette?" he asked, reaching into his pocket.','search your pocket (= look for something in your pocket ) I searched my pockets for my train ticket but it wasn''t there.','turn out/empty your pockets (= take everything out of your pockets in order to find something ) His mother made him turn out his pockets.','dig in your pocket (= put your hand in your pocket to find something ) Boris dug in his pocket for his keys.','with your hands in your pockets I saw him wandering along the beach with his hands in his pockets.','somebody''s pockets are bulging (= they are very full ) Tony''s pockets were bulging with loose change.','a back/front/side pocket He took a wad of money from his back pocket.','a breast pocket (= on the chest ) There was a silk handkerchief in his breast pocket.','an inside pocket (= on the inside of a coat, jacket etc ) Gregson pulled a photo from the inside pocket of his jacket.','a jacket/trouser/shirt etc pocket She slipped the map into her jacket pocket.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Please read the air safety card in the pocket of the seat in front.","translation":"لطفا کارت ایمنی هوا را در جیب صندلی جلو بخوانید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000342638.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('b7e9ea44-758e-5788-8516-d60c0b58522f','5b2bdbae-9a63-5b71-af76-24bf785a5ee5',4,'small area/amount','مساحت/مقدار کوچک','spoken & written','a small area or amount of something that is different from what surrounds it',null,null,'یک ناحیه یا مقدار کوچکی از چیزی که با آنچه در اطراف آن قرار دارد متفاوت است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['put something in your pocket I put the £5 note in my pocket.','stuff/thrust something in your pocket (= put it there quickly and carelessly ) He took off his cap and stuffed it in his pocket.','take something out of/from your pocket Marcia took a pair of dark glasses out of her pocket.','reach into your pocket (= put your hand into your pocket to find something ) "Do you want a cigarette?" he asked, reaching into his pocket.','search your pocket (= look for something in your pocket ) I searched my pockets for my train ticket but it wasn''t there.','turn out/empty your pockets (= take everything out of your pockets in order to find something ) His mother made him turn out his pockets.','dig in your pocket (= put your hand in your pocket to find something ) Boris dug in his pocket for his keys.','with your hands in your pockets I saw him wandering along the beach with his hands in his pockets.','somebody''s pockets are bulging (= they are very full ) Tony''s pockets were bulging with loose change.','a back/front/side pocket He took a wad of money from his back pocket.','a breast pocket (= on the chest ) There was a silk handkerchief in his breast pocket.','an inside pocket (= on the inside of a coat, jacket etc ) Gregson pulled a photo from the inside pocket of his jacket.','a jacket/trouser/shirt etc pocket She slipped the map into her jacket pocket.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"In some parts, there are still pockets of violence and unrest.","translation":"در برخی از بخش‌ها همچنان شاهد خشونت و ناآرامی است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001539505.mp3"},{"sentence":"pockets of air inside the hull of the ship","translation":"حفره های هوا در داخل بدنه کشتی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001539506.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
