('9fbccbcb-e567-559f-9c0f-504efcf05bf0','8d4d93ae-9b5d-5556-8a37-9657b93bf59a',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to put something into your pocket',null,null,'برای گذاشتن چیزی در جیبت','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Maggie locked the door and pocketed the keys.","translation":"مگی در را قفل کرد و کلیدها را در جیب گذاشت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000342716.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('f91925ed-9913-5440-94b6-07c0962eef2c','8d4d93ae-9b5d-5556-8a37-9657b93bf59a',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to steal money, especially money that you are responsible for',null,null,'برای سرقت پول، به خصوص پولی که شما مسئول آن هستید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"One inspector had pocketed up to $500,000 in bribes.","translation":"یک بازرس تا 500000 دلار رشوه به جیب زده بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001539537.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('1bfe9729-ccce-5bab-9493-309f5267e1c9','8d4d93ae-9b5d-5556-8a37-9657b93bf59a',3,null,null,'spoken & written','to get a large amount of money, win a prize etc, especially in a way that seems very easy or slightly dishonest',null,null,'به دست آوردن مقدار زیادی پول، بردن جایزه و غیره، به خصوص به روشی که بسیار آسان یا کمی نادرست به نظر می رسد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Johnston pocketed $2,500 in prize money.","translation":"جانستون مبلغ 2500 دلار جایزه به جیب زد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001539540.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('b73fa4b6-43b7-59c3-aab9-b905d3ed94a1','8d4d93ae-9b5d-5556-8a37-9657b93bf59a',4,null,null,'spoken & written','to hit a ball into a pocket in the game of pool , snooker or billiards',null,null,'زدن توپ به جیب در بازی استخر، اسنوکر یا بیلیارد',array['pot']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('080e9e02-7540-58e6-ad0d-1c869c453e37','17e18d41-0293-5387-b5aa-3e07416d5cf9',1,null,null,'spoken & written','small enough to be carried in your pocket',null,null,'آنقدر کوچک که بتوان آن را در جیب خود حمل کرد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"a pocket dictionary","translation":"دیکشنری جیبی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000342741.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('6c71586a-e7d5-5f89-9b22-073efd708238','d14afda3-3dd4-5be2-843a-46e570f958e2',1,null,null,'spoken & written','poems in general, or the art of writing them',null,null,'شعر، شاعری؛ ادبیات (شعر)؛ موسیقی (شعر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['write poetry I didn''t know you wrote poetry.','learn poetry He made us learn a lot of poetry by heart.','recite poetry (= say it to people from memory ) Occasionally, my father would recite the poetry of Baudelaire.','a piece of poetry We had to memorize a piece of poetry.','a line of poetry She often quoted lines of poetry.','a book/volume/collection of poetry He had two books of poetry published.','a poetry reading (= when poems are read to people, usually by the writer ) I used to like giving poetry readings.','a poetry book He has just brought out another poetry book.','a poetry anthology (= a book of poems by different people ) a poetry anthology containing work by modern Liverpool poets','English/French/Greek etc poetry He was a student of English poetry.','modern/contemporary poetry She finds modern poetry difficult.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He reads a lot of poetry.","translation":"او زیاد شعر می خواند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000343137.mp3"},{"sentence":"a poetry magazine","translation":"یک مجله شعر","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634649.mp3"},{"sentence":"a selection of religious poetry","translation":"گزیده ای از اشعار مذهبی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001766051.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('93d84148-e684-547b-8c38-43751a551d3b','d14afda3-3dd4-5be2-843a-46e570f958e2',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a quality of beauty , gracefulness, and deep feeling',null,null,'کیفیت زیبایی، برازندگی و احساس عمیق','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['write poetry I didn''t know you wrote poetry.','learn poetry He made us learn a lot of poetry by heart.','recite poetry (= say it to people from memory ) Occasionally, my father would recite the poetry of Baudelaire.','a piece of poetry We had to memorize a piece of poetry.','a line of poetry She often quoted lines of poetry.','a book/volume/collection of poetry He had two books of poetry published.','a poetry reading (= when poems are read to people, usually by the writer ) I used to like giving poetry readings.','a poetry book He has just brought out another poetry book.','a poetry anthology (= a book of poems by different people ) a poetry anthology containing work by modern Liverpool poets','English/French/Greek etc poetry He was a student of English poetry.','modern/contemporary poetry She finds modern poetry difficult.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The way she moves on the court is sheer poetry.","translation":"نحوه حرکت او در دادگاه شعر محض است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634654.mp3"},{"sentence":"His golf swing is poetry in motion .","translation":"تاب گلف او شعر در حرکت است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634655.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('9b8dfa68-cf12-5060-93de-29ffde29256e','37195022-1805-58c0-b16c-283255f6fc1b',1,null,null,'spoken & written','the people who work for an official organization whose job is to catch criminals and make sure that people obey the law',null,null,'پلیس، پاسبان؛ پلیس (مرکز)؛ پلیس (استان)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['call the police Staff called the police when they noticed a broken window.','tell the police ( also inform the police formal ) I think we should tell the police.','report something to the police Why are so many crimes not reported to the police?','the police investigate something Sussex Police are investigating a break-in at the club.','the police catch somebody The police are no nearer to catching his killer.','the police arrest somebody/make an arrest The police arrested Mr Fox as he tried to leave the country. Officer Singer said the police have made no arrests in the robbery.','the police question/interview somebody Police are questioning two men about the deaths.','the police charge somebody (= officially say that someone will be judged in a court for committing a crime ) The police have charged the parents with murder.','the police hold somebody ( also the police detain somebody formal ) (= keep them at a police station ) The police can hold suspects for up to 48 hours without charge. The police detained several activists, but released them after questioning.','the police release somebody The police released William and all charges were dropped.','the police appeal for something Police are appealing for witnesses to the attack.','the police raid/storm a place The police raided his home and took his computer.','armed police Armed police surrounded the house.','uniformed police Uniformed police and plain clothes detectives were present in large numbers.','riot police Riot police moved in with tear gas.','traffic police British English Traffic police closed the motorway after the accident.','a police investigation Despite a police investigation, no arrests were made.','a police raid (= a surprise visit made by the police to search for something illegal ) Six people were arrested in a police raid on the bar.','a police escort (= a police officer or officers that go with someone to guard or protect them ) The teams will parade through the city with a police escort.','a police cordon (= a line of police officers who are preventing people going somewhere ) The demonstrators tried to break through a police cordon.','the police force Her son is in the police force.','a police officer The police officer asked to see his driving licence.','a police station (= building where the police work ) They took him down to the police station to ask him some questions.','a police car The men were being followed by an unmarked police car.','a police dog Police dogs were used to catch the thieves.','police brutality/harassment (= when the police hit or threaten people ) He claims to have witnessed many instances of police brutality.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Police surrounded the courthouse.","translation":"پلیس ساختمان دادگاه را محاصره کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000345337.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('9a1e11c3-871d-5b97-baa3-cf49227c0ec6','37195022-1805-58c0-b16c-283255f6fc1b',2,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'the police','پلیس، پاسبان؛ پلیس (مرکز)؛ پلیس (استان)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['call the police Staff called the police when they noticed a broken window.','tell the police ( also inform the police formal ) I think we should tell the police.','report something to the police Why are so many crimes not reported to the police?','the police investigate something Sussex Police are investigating a break-in at the club.','the police catch somebody The police are no nearer to catching his killer.','the police arrest somebody/make an arrest The police arrested Mr Fox as he tried to leave the country. Officer Singer said the police have made no arrests in the robbery.','the police question/interview somebody Police are questioning two men about the deaths.','the police charge somebody (= officially say that someone will be judged in a court for committing a crime ) The police have charged the parents with murder.','the police hold somebody ( also the police detain somebody formal ) (= keep them at a police station ) The police can hold suspects for up to 48 hours without charge. The police detained several activists, but released them after questioning.','the police release somebody The police released William and all charges were dropped.','the police appeal for something Police are appealing for witnesses to the attack.','the police raid/storm a place The police raided his home and took his computer.','armed police Armed police surrounded the house.','uniformed police Uniformed police and plain clothes detectives were present in large numbers.','riot police Riot police moved in with tear gas.','traffic police British English Traffic police closed the motorway after the accident.','a police investigation Despite a police investigation, no arrests were made.','a police raid (= a surprise visit made by the police to search for something illegal ) Six people were arrested in a police raid on the bar.','a police escort (= a police officer or officers that go with someone to guard or protect them ) The teams will parade through the city with a police escort.','a police cordon (= a line of police officers who are preventing people going somewhere ) The demonstrators tried to break through a police cordon.','the police force Her son is in the police force.','a police officer The police officer asked to see his driving licence.','a police station (= building where the police work ) They took him down to the police station to ask him some questions.','a police car The men were being followed by an unmarked police car.','a police dog Police dogs were used to catch the thieves.','police brutality/harassment (= when the police hit or threaten people ) He claims to have witnessed many instances of police brutality.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('dab620d1-fdcd-5474-a01b-569d21e31aff','95ce6fdb-d108-5cff-9d1a-9ade3c969ec6',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to keep control over a particular area in order to make sure that laws are obeyed and that people and property are protected , using a police or military force',null,null,'برای اطمینان از رعایت قوانین و حفاظت از افراد و اموال، با استفاده از نیروی پلیس یا نظامی، کنترل یک منطقه خاص را حفظ کنید.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The army was brought in to police the city centre.","translation":"ارتش برای پلیس مرکز شهر آورده شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000345356.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('72840efb-7ae3-5c7f-bc29-87dd169835b1','95ce6fdb-d108-5cff-9d1a-9ade3c969ec6',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to control a particular activity or industry by making sure that people follow the correct rules for what they do',null,null,'برای کنترل یک فعالیت یا صنعت خاص با اطمینان از اینکه افراد از قوانین صحیح کاری که انجام می دهند پیروی می کنند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"The agency was set up to police the nuclear power industry.","translation":"این آژانس برای پلیس صنعت انرژی هسته ای راه اندازی شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000345362.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('faaf547e-0655-52e1-991d-e7bfbee18cea','5d5336ac-564c-5f3d-9f7b-a4e976e21264',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a way of doing something that has been officially agreed and chosen by a political party , a business, or another organization','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'سیاست، خط مشی؛ مقررات (شرکت)؛ بیمه (پول)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['government/public/state policy Government spending is determined by government policy.','party policy State ownership is party policy.','company/hospital/university etc policy It is not company policy to offer refunds.','foreign policy Support for human rights is a key element in our foreign policy.','economic/fiscal policy The middle classes have suffered most as a result of government economic policies.','defence/energy/housing etc policy Our energy policies must put the environment first.','a deliberate policy Some customers pursue a deliberate policy of delaying payment.','a clear policy There was no clear policy on this matter.','a coherent policy (= one in which all the parts of the policy work well together ) A long-term coherent policy for industry is needed.','formulate/develop a policy We try to formulate policies that will meet the needs of the people.','make policy (= decide what it will be ) A committee of representatives makes policy.','shape policy (= develop it or have an influence on it ) These terrorist acts will not be allowed to shape our foreign policy.','adopt a policy (= use one ) He adopted a policy of radical reform.','implement a policy (= take action in the way that has been decided ) Local government is responsible for implementing central government policy.','pursue/follow a policy (= continue with a policy over a period of time ) The organization is pursuing a policy of cost cutting.','reverse a policy (= stop a policy and change it ) The new government set about reversing previous policies.','a policy aims at something/to do something (= tries to achieve something ) The policy aimed to reduce the budget deficit.','a policy decision No policy decision can be made until the next meeting.','a policy statement There has been no policy statement on this from the French government.','a policy change There have been numerous policy changes in recent months.','a policy issue He rarely consulted him on general policy issues.','a policy maker (= someone who decides on what it should be ) Policy makers have not dealt with the issue very effectively.','a policy objective How can we best achieve our policy objectives?','a policy initiative (= something done to achieve a policy''s goals ) The policy initiatives have focused on the inner cities.','a change of/in policy This decision represented a major change in policy.','a shift in policy (= a small change ) The shift in policy placed more emphasis on teachers'' assessments of students'' progress.','a reversal of policy (= a change back to what it was before ) The strength of this opposition forced a rapid reversal of policy.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"a foreign policy adviser","translation":"یک مشاور سیاست خارجی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634527.mp3"},{"sentence":"The company has adopted a strict no-smoking policy.","translation":"این شرکت یک سیاست سختگیرانه برای ممنوعیت سیگار را اتخاذ کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634528.mp3"},{"sentence":"government policy on higher education","translation":"سیاست دولت در مورد آموزش عالی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000345502.mp3"},{"sentence":"US policy towards China","translation":"سیاست آمریکا در قبال چین","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634534.mp3"},{"sentence":"It is hospital policy to screen all mothers with certain risk factors.","translation":"این سیاست بیمارستانی است که همه مادران را با عوامل خطر خاص غربالگری کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001842872.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('97a62416-9686-5e3a-a5ea-f5fb84a21282','5d5336ac-564c-5f3d-9f7b-a4e976e21264',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a contract with an insurance company, or an official written statement giving all the details of such a contract','[ countable ]',null,'قرارداد با یک شرکت بیمه، یا یک بیانیه کتبی رسمی که تمام جزئیات چنین قراردادی را ارائه می دهد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"an insurance policy","translation":"یک بیمه نامه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634535.mp3"},{"sentence":"There’s a clause in the policy that I’d like to discuss.","translation":"یک بند در سیاست وجود دارد که من می خواهم در مورد آن بحث کنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634538.mp3"},{"sentence":"I’ve just renewed the policy (= arranged for it to continue ) .","translation":"من به تازگی این خط مشی را تمدید کردم (= ترتیبی دادم تا ادامه یابد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634539.mp3"},{"sentence":"Does the policy cover theft and fire?","translation":"آیا این بیمه نامه شامل سرقت و آتش سوزی می شود؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634546.mp3"},{"sentence":"You can take out a policy (= buy one ) for as little as $11.00 a month.","translation":"شما می توانید یک بیمه نامه (= خرید یک ) با کمتر از 11 دلار در ماه بگیرید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634550.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('18845168-e48a-5df1-8cc8-aa1cad63e293','5d5336ac-564c-5f3d-9f7b-a4e976e21264',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a particular principle that you believe in and that influences the way you behave','[ countable ]',null,'اصل خاصی که به آن اعتقاد دارید و بر نحوه رفتار شما تأثیر می گذارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"It’s always been my policy not to gossip.","translation":"همیشه سیاست من این بوده که شایعه نکنم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001766103.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('d9428ac9-f553-596a-9971-d171cf88a56e','bf837705-0a95-5f4c-9782-fd15c30d6d33',1,null,null,'spoken & written','behaving or speaking in a way that is correct for the social situation you are in, and showing that you are careful to consider other people’s needs and feelings',null,null,'مؤدب، باادب؛ مودبانه (حرف)؛ خوش‌برخورد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"She’s always very polite.","translation":"او همیشه بسیار مودب است","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001766112.mp3"},{"sentence":"polite, well-behaved children","translation":"بچه های مودب و خوش رفتار","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634597.mp3"},{"sentence":"a clear but polite request","translation":"یک درخواست واضح اما مودبانه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001766113.mp3"},{"sentence":"We left the party as soon as it was polite to do so.","translation":"به محض اینکه مودبانه بود، مهمانی را ترک کردیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000345723.mp3"},{"sentence":"It’s not polite to talk with your mouth full.","translation":"مودبانه نیست که با دهان پر صحبت کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000345724.mp3"}]'::jsonb,5),
('161214af-6e24-5ff6-830b-9478ab3d83f9','bf837705-0a95-5f4c-9782-fd15c30d6d33',2,null,null,'spoken & written','you make polite conversation , remarks etc because it is considered socially correct to do this, but not necessarily because you believe what you are saying',null,null,'شما مکالمه مودبانه، اظهارات و غیره انجام می دهید زیرا از نظر اجتماعی انجام این کار صحیح تلقی می شود، اما نه لزوماً به این دلیل که به آنچه می گویید اعتقاد دارید.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"While they ate, they made polite conversation about the weather.","translation":"در حین غذا خوردن، صحبت های مؤدبانه ای درباره آب و هوا انجام دادند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634600.mp3"},{"sentence":"Jan expressed polite interest in Edward’s stamp collection.","translation":"جان به مجموعه تمبرهای ادوارد ابراز علاقه کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634601.mp3"},{"sentence":"I know Ian said he liked her singing, but he was only being polite .","translation":"می دانم که ایان گفت از آواز خواندن او خوشش می آید، اما او فقط مودب بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001634602.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('894f14f8-193e-5216-ae60-4d4a394de587','bf837705-0a95-5f4c-9782-fd15c30d6d33',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'in polite society/circles/company','مؤدب، باادب؛ مودبانه (حرف)؛ خوش‌برخورد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('edf0de1d-1193-55fc-b838-910c44908c1d','fb99f18e-b01e-53af-ba0e-1f483b8d7b1f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a large printed notice , picture, or photograph , used to advertise something or as a decoration',null,null,'پوستر، اعلان (دیوار)؛ پوستر (تبلیغ)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"A team of volunteers were putting up posters .","translation":"تیمی از داوطلبان در حال نصب پوستر بودند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000313386.mp3"},{"sentence":"a poster campaign for the election","translation":"تبلیغات پوستری برای انتخابات","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001577023.mp3"},{"sentence":"the poster for the exhibition","translation":"پوستر نمایشگاه","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001577019.mp3"},{"sentence":"posters of old movie stars","translation":"پوسترهای ستاره های قدیمی سینما","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001577022.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('ea119eca-250f-5f6a-bc14-fe2c586919ba','5338b1d7-df9f-50ce-8b95-9e031f478b0f',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a round white vegetable with a brown , red, or pale yellow skin , that grows under the ground','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'سیب‌زمینی، آلو (نمک)؛ سیب‌زمینی (سرخ‌کرده)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['peel potatoes (= cut the skin off them ) Peel and slice the potatoes.','slice potatoes (= cut them into long thin pieces )','dice potatoes (= cut them into small square pieces )','mash potatoes (= crush them until they are smooth, after boiling them )','boiled potatoes Serve with plain boiled potatoes.','mashed potato(es) (= boiled and crushed until smooth ) I like sausages with mashed potatoes.','roast potatoes (= cooked in an oven with fat ) traditional roast beef with roast potatoes','a baked/jacket potato (= cooked in its skin ) We cooked baked potatoes in the embers of the fire.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Marie stood at the sink, peeling potatoes (= cutting off the skin ) .","translation":"ماری کنار سینک ایستاده بود و سیب زمینی را پوست می گرفت (= پوستش را می برد).","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001665123.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('9977ab03-b81d-50ed-8f87-46bf0ebd25fe','5338b1d7-df9f-50ce-8b95-9e031f478b0f',2,null,null,'spoken & written','a plant that produces potatoes','[ countable ]',null,'گیاهی که سیب زمینی تولید می کند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['peel potatoes (= cut the skin off them ) Peel and slice the potatoes.','slice potatoes (= cut them into long thin pieces )','dice potatoes (= cut them into small square pieces )','mash potatoes (= crush them until they are smooth, after boiling them )','boiled potatoes Serve with plain boiled potatoes.','mashed potato(es) (= boiled and crushed until smooth ) I like sausages with mashed potatoes.','roast potatoes (= cooked in an oven with fat ) traditional roast beef with roast potatoes','a baked/jacket potato (= cooked in its skin ) We cooked baked potatoes in the embers of the fire.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('c7129857-3a41-5a98-ab51-62bdbaaa9547','8c20194c-f2c4-5380-af58-d5bbaa1bba61',1,null,null,'spoken & written','to say that you admire and approve of someone or something, especially publicly',null,null,'گفتن اینکه شما شخص یا چیزی را تحسین و تایید می کنید، به خصوص در علنا','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Jane was praised by her teacher.","translation":"جین توسط معلمش مورد تحسین قرار گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000318269.mp3"},{"sentence":"The mayor praised the rescue teams for their courage.","translation":"شهردار از تیم های امدادی به خاطر شجاعتشان تقدیر کرد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000318272.mp3"},{"sentence":"a highly praised novel","translation":"یک رمان بسیار تحسین شده","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000318275.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('abada252-4350-5af6-b4e8-02a907a89e2f','8c20194c-f2c4-5380-af58-d5bbaa1bba61',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to give thanks to God and show your respect to Him, especially by singing in a church',null,null,'خدا را شکر کنید و به او احترام بگذارید، به ویژه با آواز خواندن در کلیسا','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('60a8ce41-af29-5a25-a09c-af503d4e4cc0','8c20194c-f2c4-5380-af58-d5bbaa1bba61',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'God/Heaven be praised',null,'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('01e8780a-0037-5490-8963-0beae69a4763','367c2c1e-96c3-5100-8d01-fdf1f6861dd3',1,null,null,'spoken & written','words that you say or write in order to praise someone or something',null,null,'ستایش، تحسین؛ درود (خدا)؛ ستایش (خدا)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['give somebody praise Give your dog plenty of praise when it behaves well.','get praise His actions did not get the praise they deserved.','win/earn/receive praise The trade deal won praise from the American business community.','deserve praise She deserves praise for all the charity work she does.','be singled out for praise (= be the one person who is praised ) His work was singled out for praise by the examiners.','heap/lavish praise on somebody (= praise them a lot ) Ireland''s manager has heaped praise on his team.','shower somebody with praise (= praise them a lot ) Taiwan''s media lately showered praise on Li Yundi, the 18-year-old piano prodigy.','high praise (= a lot of praise ) The film won high praise from critics and audiences alike.','special praise My sister was constantly singled out for special praise.','lavish praise (= very high praise ) United’s captain received lavish praise from his manager.','faint praise (= comments that seem to praise someone, but in a way that does not really give them much praise ) He wins faint praise as ‘the only candidate with a grain of sense’.','be full of praise for somebody (= praise them a lot ) Captain Jones was full of praise for his men.','have nothing but praise for somebody/something (= praise them a lot, especially when they have had to deal with a difficult situation ) Passengers had nothing but praise for the pilot.','words of praise She still had some words of praise for her ex-husband’s wit and charm.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"It''s important to give children plenty of praise and encouragement.","translation":"بسیار مهم است که کودکان را تحسین و تشویق کنید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040176.mp3"},{"sentence":"Her teacher was full of praise for her work.","translation":"معلم او برای کار او پر از ستایش بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040177.mp3"},{"sentence":"His first novel received high praise .","translation":"اولین رمان او مورد تحسین قرار گرفت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000318305.mp3"},{"sentence":"Gregory was singled out (= he was chosen in particular ) for special praise .","translation":"گریگوری را برای ستایش خاص برگزیدند (= او را خاص برگزیدند .","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa040178.mp3"},{"sentence":"The film has won praise from audiences and critics alike.","translation":"این فیلم مورد تحسین تماشاگران و منتقدان قرار گرفته است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000318309.mp3"},{"sentence":"He wrote a poem in praise of his hero.","translation":"او شعری در مدح قهرمانش سروده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001240.mp3"}]'::jsonb,6),
('492987db-06f0-5cd7-ab4d-773183351959','367c2c1e-96c3-5100-8d01-fdf1f6861dd3',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the expression of respect and thanks to God',null,null,'ابراز احترام و تشکر از خداوند','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['give somebody praise Give your dog plenty of praise when it behaves well.','get praise His actions did not get the praise they deserved.','win/earn/receive praise The trade deal won praise from the American business community.','deserve praise She deserves praise for all the charity work she does.','be singled out for praise (= be the one person who is praised ) His work was singled out for praise by the examiners.','heap/lavish praise on somebody (= praise them a lot ) Ireland''s manager has heaped praise on his team.','shower somebody with praise (= praise them a lot ) Taiwan''s media lately showered praise on Li Yundi, the 18-year-old piano prodigy.','high praise (= a lot of praise ) The film won high praise from critics and audiences alike.','special praise My sister was constantly singled out for special praise.','lavish praise (= very high praise ) United’s captain received lavish praise from his manager.','faint praise (= comments that seem to praise someone, but in a way that does not really give them much praise ) He wins faint praise as ‘the only candidate with a grain of sense’.','be full of praise for somebody (= praise them a lot ) Captain Jones was full of praise for his men.','have nothing but praise for somebody/something (= praise them a lot, especially when they have had to deal with a difficult situation ) Passengers had nothing but praise for the pilot.','words of praise She still had some words of praise for her ex-husband’s wit and charm.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Let us give praise unto the Lord.","translation":"خداوند را ستایش کنیم.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000318314.mp3"},{"sentence":"songs of praise","translation":"آهنگ های ستایش","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001568062.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('04bfe1d9-cdfd-53f6-a7a8-c63b3affb243','367c2c1e-96c3-5100-8d01-fdf1f6861dd3',3,null,null,'spoken & written',null,null,'praise be!','ستایش، تحسین؛ درود (خدا)؛ ستایش (خدا)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['give somebody praise Give your dog plenty of praise when it behaves well.','get praise His actions did not get the praise they deserved.','win/earn/receive praise The trade deal won praise from the American business community.','deserve praise She deserves praise for all the charity work she does.','be singled out for praise (= be the one person who is praised ) His work was singled out for praise by the examiners.','heap/lavish praise on somebody (= praise them a lot ) Ireland''s manager has heaped praise on his team.','shower somebody with praise (= praise them a lot ) Taiwan''s media lately showered praise on Li Yundi, the 18-year-old piano prodigy.','high praise (= a lot of praise ) The film won high praise from critics and audiences alike.','special praise My sister was constantly singled out for special praise.','lavish praise (= very high praise ) United’s captain received lavish praise from his manager.','faint praise (= comments that seem to praise someone, but in a way that does not really give them much praise ) He wins faint praise as ‘the only candidate with a grain of sense’.','be full of praise for somebody (= praise them a lot ) Captain Jones was full of praise for his men.','have nothing but praise for somebody/something (= praise them a lot, especially when they have had to deal with a difficult situation ) Passengers had nothing but praise for the pilot.','words of praise She still had some words of praise for her ex-husband’s wit and charm.']::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('1132907a-1bab-5c09-b4e8-b51b79a15e18','510ebdf0-13ba-569c-9616-bf2ff63c27d2',1,null,null,'spoken & written','words that you say when praying to God or gods','[ countable ]','Lord''s Prayer','دعا، نیایش؛ اعتراف (دعا)؛ دعا (یواشکی)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['say a prayer Say a prayer for me.','utter a prayer formal (= say a prayer ) When she recovered, she uttered a prayer of thanks.','offer a prayer (= say a prayer in a formal way, often in a group ) Special prayers were offered for the boys during a service yesterday.','hear somebody''s prayer God must have heard my prayers.','answer somebody''s prayer (= respond to a prayer, especially by giving you what you ask for ) One day my prayers were answered.','be in somebody''s prayers (= be prayed for ) You are always in my prayers.','a silent prayer He said a silent prayer as he walked.','a prayer book (= book containing prayers )','a prayer mat/rug (= small cloth on which Muslims kneel to pray )','a prayer meeting (= meeting at which people pray together )','a prayer service (= church service at which people pray )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Our thoughts and prayers are with you at this difficult time.","translation":"افکار و دعاهای ما در این زمان سخت همراه شماست.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000319081.mp3"},{"sentence":"The children said their prayers and got into bed.","translation":"بچه ها نماز خواندند و به رختخواب رفتند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001568400.mp3"},{"sentence":"God has answered your prayer .","translation":"خداوند دعای شما را مستجاب کرده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001568406.mp3"},{"sentence":"a prayer for the dead","translation":"دعایی برای اموات","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000319084.mp3"}]'::jsonb,4),
('7423454c-4cd9-51c0-bb3f-741e227aecd0','510ebdf0-13ba-569c-9616-bf2ff63c27d2',2,null,null,'spoken & written','when someone prays, or the regular habit of praying','[ uncountable ]',null,'وقتی کسی نماز می خواند یا عادت همیشگی دعا کردن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['say a prayer Say a prayer for me.','utter a prayer formal (= say a prayer ) When she recovered, she uttered a prayer of thanks.','offer a prayer (= say a prayer in a formal way, often in a group ) Special prayers were offered for the boys during a service yesterday.','hear somebody''s prayer God must have heard my prayers.','answer somebody''s prayer (= respond to a prayer, especially by giving you what you ask for ) One day my prayers were answered.','be in somebody''s prayers (= be prayed for ) You are always in my prayers.','a silent prayer He said a silent prayer as he walked.','a prayer book (= book containing prayers )','a prayer mat/rug (= small cloth on which Muslims kneel to pray )','a prayer meeting (= meeting at which people pray together )','a prayer service (= church service at which people pray )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the power of prayer","translation":"قدرت دعا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000319090.mp3"},{"sentence":"a prayer meeting","translation":"یک جلسه دعا","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000319091.mp3"},{"sentence":"The congregation knelt in prayer.","translation":"جماعت به نماز زانو زدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000319095.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('967f6bb4-cd74-5ee6-b66c-ca2ed65047de','510ebdf0-13ba-569c-9616-bf2ff63c27d2',3,null,null,'spoken & written','a wish or hope that something will happen','[ countable ]',null,'آرزو یا امید به اینکه اتفاقی بیفتد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['say a prayer Say a prayer for me.','utter a prayer formal (= say a prayer ) When she recovered, she uttered a prayer of thanks.','offer a prayer (= say a prayer in a formal way, often in a group ) Special prayers were offered for the boys during a service yesterday.','hear somebody''s prayer God must have heard my prayers.','answer somebody''s prayer (= respond to a prayer, especially by giving you what you ask for ) One day my prayers were answered.','be in somebody''s prayers (= be prayed for ) You are always in my prayers.','a silent prayer He said a silent prayer as he walked.','a prayer book (= book containing prayers )','a prayer mat/rug (= small cloth on which Muslims kneel to pray )','a prayer meeting (= meeting at which people pray together )','a prayer service (= church service at which people pray )']::text[],'[{"sentence":"Her prayer was that she would pass her exams.","translation":"دعایش این بود که امتحاناتش را پس بدهد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000319101.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
