('8251ec88-8d93-5335-993e-fb5f75e9a7c3','1ae2d629-7d79-58db-900c-d30fe063c776',1,null,null,'spoken & written','(1958–) a US singer , guitar player , and songwriter , who is known for dressing and performing in a way that is intended to be sexually exciting and shocking . He was one of the most successful singers of the 1980s, and his records include Purple Rain (1984) and Sign O'' the Times (1987).',null,null,'(1958-) یک خواننده، نوازنده گیتار و ترانه سرای آمریکایی، که به دلیل لباس پوشیدن و اجرای شیوه ای که از نظر جنسی هیجان انگیز و تکان دهنده باشد، مشهور است. او یکی از موفق ترین خوانندگان دهه 1980 بود و از سوابق او می توان به باران بنفش (1984) و Sign O'' the Times (1987) اشاره کرد.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('14931afe-9896-5221-a563-f3038ef982a6','adf5eb59-f8cb-50b1-9e0e-6dc390e774a3',1,null,null,'spoken & written','(1532) a book by Machiavelli which discusses what a ruler should do in order to gain and keep power and be an effective ruler, even if this means being cruel , dishonest or immoral',null,null,'(1532) کتابی از ماکیاولی که در مورد آنچه که یک حاکم باید برای به دست آوردن و حفظ قدرت و یک حاکم مؤثر انجام دهد، بحث می کند، حتی اگر این به معنای ظالم، ناصادق یا غیراخلاقی باشد.','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[]'::jsonb,0),
('960b59ef-fc7b-5748-867b-e7303fca9e15','ac061114-b52b-5e7c-a505-b870602a5aea',1,null,null,'spoken & written','a building where people are kept as a punishment for a crime , or while they are waiting to go to court for their trial','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'زندان، حبس؛ زندان (شکل)',array['jail']::text[],'{}'::text[],array['go to prison She went to prison for theft.','put somebody in prison Mentally ill people should not be put in prison.','send somebody to prison I was afraid I might get sent to prison.','be released from prison He was released from prison six weeks ago.','let somebody out of prison When’s he going to be let out of prison?','come/get out of prison The boy just come out of prison after doing two years for assault.','escape from (a) prison Blake escaped from a Missouri prison last year.','an open prison (= one where prisoners are not restricted as much as usual ) He was transferred to an open prison.','a maximum security prison He was sent to a maximum security prison where prisoners are kept in their cells almost 23 hours a day.','a prison sentence/term (= a period of time in prison as a punishment ) He is serving a four-year prison sentence.','a prison officer/official/warder/guard Last month, a prisoner attacked two prison officers with a knife.','a prison cell (= a room where a prisoner lives ) Overcrowding means that many prisoners have to share a prison cell.','the prison population (= all the prisoners in a country ) The government wants to reduce the size of the prison population.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"He visits his dad in prison every week.","translation":"او هر هفته با پدرش در زندان ملاقات می کند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001568904.mp3"},{"sentence":"Ricky has been out of prison for three years now.","translation":"ریکی سه سال است که از زندان بیرون آمده است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa020187.mp3"},{"sentence":"They’ll probably put him in prison for a long time.","translation":"احتمالاً او را برای مدت طولانی در زندان خواهند انداخت.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001941788.mp3"},{"sentence":"Helen was sent to prison for attacking a man with a knife.","translation":"هلن به دلیل حمله به مردی با چاقو روانه زندان شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001568921.mp3"},{"sentence":"The two men were arrested only a week after they were released from prison .","translation":"این دو مرد تنها یک هفته پس از آزادی از زندان دستگیر شدند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001568925.mp3"},{"sentence":"Three terrorists escaped from Brixton Prison .","translation":"سه تروریست از زندان بریکستون فرار کردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001568929.mp3"},{"sentence":"an increase in the number of women going to prison","translation":"افزایش تعداد زنان زندانی","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001568917.mp3"},{"sentence":"Mr Gunn received a ten-year prison sentence .","translation":"آقای گان به ده سال زندان محکوم شد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00682.mp3"}]'::jsonb,8),
('2a7379a6-2ce8-5213-ab96-e2fcb704d2ca','ac061114-b52b-5e7c-a505-b870602a5aea',2,null,null,'spoken & written','the system that deals with keeping people in a prison','[ uncountable ]',null,'سیستمی که با نگهداری افراد در زندان سروکار دارد','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['go to prison She went to prison for theft.','put somebody in prison Mentally ill people should not be put in prison.','send somebody to prison I was afraid I might get sent to prison.','be released from prison He was released from prison six weeks ago.','let somebody out of prison When’s he going to be let out of prison?','come/get out of prison The boy just come out of prison after doing two years for assault.','escape from (a) prison Blake escaped from a Missouri prison last year.','an open prison (= one where prisoners are not restricted as much as usual ) He was transferred to an open prison.','a maximum security prison He was sent to a maximum security prison where prisoners are kept in their cells almost 23 hours a day.','a prison sentence/term (= a period of time in prison as a punishment ) He is serving a four-year prison sentence.','a prison officer/official/warder/guard Last month, a prisoner attacked two prison officers with a knife.','a prison cell (= a room where a prisoner lives ) Overcrowding means that many prisoners have to share a prison cell.','the prison population (= all the prisoners in a country ) The government wants to reduce the size of the prison population.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"the prison service","translation":"سرویس زندان","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001825667.mp3"},{"sentence":"Does prison deter criminals from offending again?","translation":"آیا زندان مجرمان را از ارتکاب مجدد باز می دارد؟","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000293619.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('b549c840-148d-5470-b714-075eb636ba00','ac061114-b52b-5e7c-a505-b870602a5aea',3,null,null,'spoken & written','an unpleasant place or situation which it is difficult to escape from','[ countable ]',null,'مکان یا موقعیت ناخوشایندی که فرار از آن دشوار است','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['go to prison She went to prison for theft.','put somebody in prison Mentally ill people should not be put in prison.','send somebody to prison I was afraid I might get sent to prison.','be released from prison He was released from prison six weeks ago.','let somebody out of prison When’s he going to be let out of prison?','come/get out of prison The boy just come out of prison after doing two years for assault.','escape from (a) prison Blake escaped from a Missouri prison last year.','an open prison (= one where prisoners are not restricted as much as usual ) He was transferred to an open prison.','a maximum security prison He was sent to a maximum security prison where prisoners are kept in their cells almost 23 hours a day.','a prison sentence/term (= a period of time in prison as a punishment ) He is serving a four-year prison sentence.','a prison officer/official/warder/guard Last month, a prisoner attacked two prison officers with a knife.','a prison cell (= a room where a prisoner lives ) Overcrowding means that many prisoners have to share a prison cell.','the prison population (= all the prisoners in a country ) The government wants to reduce the size of the prison population.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The farm felt like a prison to her.","translation":"مزرعه برای او مانند یک زندان بود.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce6exa_00683.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('d70b19d3-0786-5b1c-b0e5-bd35e6d5dcce','e6f04dad-fb0c-5c5d-af98-dfe7f4604230',1,null,null,'spoken & written','money that you gain by selling things or doing business , after your costs have been paid','[ countable, uncountable ]',null,'سود، بهره (مالی)؛ منفعت (خیر)','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a big/huge profit Drug companies make huge profits.','a quick profit (= happening quickly ) They were only interested in a quick profit.','a good profit There is a good profit to be made in selling cars.','a substantial profit The agent then sells the land for a substantial profit to someone else.','a healthy/handsome/tidy profit (= big ) By the second year, the restaurant began to make a healthy profit.','a small/modest profit The business managed to produce a small profit last year.','net profit (= after tax and costs are paid ) The company made a net profit of $10.5 million.','gross profit ( also pre-tax profit ) (= before tax and costs are paid ) The hotel group made a gross profit of £51.9 million in 2008.','trading/operating profit (= profit relating to a company’s normal activities ) Both turnover and operating profits were lower.','make a profit We are in business to make a profit.','turn/earn a profit (= make a profit ) Without the liquor sales, the store could not turn a profit.','show a profit (= make a profit ) The business will not show a profit this year.','report/post a profit (= officially announce a profit ) The company reported net profits of $3.6 million for fiscal year 2006.','generate profit(s) We have the capacity to generate more profit.','boost profits (= make them increase ) They aim to boost profits by slashing costs.','maximize profits (= make them as big as possible ) Every firm tries to maximize its profits.','profits are up/down Pre-tax profits were up 21.5%.','profits rise/increase/grow Half of the firms surveyed expected profits to rise.','profits soar/leap (= increase by a large amount )','profits fall The group saw profits fall from £24m to £17.8m.','profits slump/plunge (= fall by a large amount ) The group’s pre-tax profits slumped to £25.5m.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"The shop’s daily profit is usually around $500.","translation":"سود روزانه فروشگاه معمولاً حدود 500 دلار است.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/ldoce5_exa001251.mp3"},{"sentence":"She sold the business and bought a farm with the profits.","translation":"او تجارت را فروخت و با سود آن مزرعه ای خرید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001574843.mp3"},{"sentence":"They sold their house at a healthy profit .","translation":"آنها خانه خود را با سود سالم فروختند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001574847.mp3"}]'::jsonb,3),
('602c89bb-4670-54c0-8d40-72979b05188b','e6f04dad-fb0c-5c5d-af98-dfe7f4604230',2,null,null,'formal','an advantage that you gain from doing something','[ uncountable ]',null,'مزیتی که از انجام کاری به دست می آورید','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],array['a big/huge profit Drug companies make huge profits.','a quick profit (= happening quickly ) They were only interested in a quick profit.','a good profit There is a good profit to be made in selling cars.','a substantial profit The agent then sells the land for a substantial profit to someone else.','a healthy/handsome/tidy profit (= big ) By the second year, the restaurant began to make a healthy profit.','a small/modest profit The business managed to produce a small profit last year.','net profit (= after tax and costs are paid ) The company made a net profit of $10.5 million.','gross profit ( also pre-tax profit ) (= before tax and costs are paid ) The hotel group made a gross profit of £51.9 million in 2008.','trading/operating profit (= profit relating to a company’s normal activities ) Both turnover and operating profits were lower.','make a profit We are in business to make a profit.','turn/earn a profit (= make a profit ) Without the liquor sales, the store could not turn a profit.','show a profit (= make a profit ) The business will not show a profit this year.','report/post a profit (= officially announce a profit ) The company reported net profits of $3.6 million for fiscal year 2006.','generate profit(s) We have the capacity to generate more profit.','boost profits (= make them increase ) They aim to boost profits by slashing costs.','maximize profits (= make them as big as possible ) Every firm tries to maximize its profits.','profits are up/down Pre-tax profits were up 21.5%.','profits rise/increase/grow Half of the firms surveyed expected profits to rise.','profits soar/leap (= increase by a large amount )','profits fall The group saw profits fall from £24m to £17.8m.','profits slump/plunge (= fall by a large amount ) The group’s pre-tax profits slumped to £25.5m.']::text[],'[{"sentence":"There’s no profit in letting meetings drag on.","translation":"هیچ سودی در ادامه دادن جلسات وجود ندارد.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-000298724.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
('dab00309-324f-5ac0-964c-d9c9e1f2eca2','6224f24d-aa76-560f-a2da-bc818fbcb17a',1,null,null,'formal','to be useful or helpful to someone',null,null,'برای کسی مفید یا مفید بودن','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"It might profit you to learn about the company before your interview.","translation":"ممکن است برای شما مفید باشد که قبل از مصاحبه با شرکت آشنا شوید.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001770760.mp3"},{"sentence":"There are lessons in these stories that all children can profit by.","translation":"در این داستان ها درس هایی وجود دارد که همه کودکان می توانند از آنها سود ببرند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001574873.mp3"}]'::jsonb,2),
('435a9316-1781-59ae-853b-8599bed24484','6224f24d-aa76-560f-a2da-bc818fbcb17a',2,null,null,'spoken & written','to get money from doing something',null,null,'برای بدست آوردن پول از انجام کاری','{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'[{"sentence":"Some industries, such as shipbuilding, clearly profited from the war.","translation":"برخی از صنایع، مانند کشتی سازی، آشکارا از جنگ سود بردند.","audio_url":"https://www.ldoceonline.com/media/english/exaProns/p008-001574879.mp3"}]'::jsonb,1),
